---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Hormuz Watch"
  description="What Hormuz Watch is, what it is not, technology credits and disclaimers."
  currentPath="/about"
>
  <div class="mb-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white">About Hormuz Watch</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-400">A demonstration shipping-intelligence dashboard for the Strait of Hormuz.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="panel panel-pad mb-6" aria-labelledby="what-it-is">
    <h2 id="what-it-is" class="card-title">What it is</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      Hormuz Watch is a <strong class="text-white">demonstration dashboard</strong> that shows how a
      shipping-intelligence interface for a strategic maritime chokepoint can be built: vessel
      tracking views, shipping routes, oil price charts, war-risk insurance indicators, news feeds,
      incident timelines and regional impact assessments — all with explicit data-quality labels.
      It is a teaching and portfolio project: the architecture demonstrates a provider layer that
      gracefully degrades from live APIs to clearly-labelled demo data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel panel-pad mb-6" aria-labelledby="what-it-is-not">
    <h2 id="what-it-is-not" class="card-title">What it is not</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      It is <strong class="text-white">not</strong> a real-time intelligence feed, a trading tool, a
      navigation aid, or a source of verified news. Vessel positions are fictional, price series are
      simulated, timeline incidents are invented scenarios, and insurance figures are illustrative
      estimates. Nothing here should inform commercial, navigational or safety-critical decisions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel panel-pad mb-6" aria-labelledby="tech">
    <h2 id="tech" class="card-title">Technology credits</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-sm text-slate-300 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <li><strong class="text-white">Astro</strong> — static site generation and page routing</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Svelte 5</strong> — interactive islands and UI state</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Tailwind CSS</strong> — utility-first styling</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Leaflet</strong> — interactive vessel map</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Chart.js</strong> — oil price charts</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">CARTO / OpenStreetMap</strong> — dark map basemap tiles</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">GDELT 2.1</strong> — optional keyless live news API</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
      <strong class="text-white">Original branding note:</strong> this project's scope is inspired by
      the general idea of a public maritime-monitoring reference, but all branding, copy, scenarios
      and data on Hormuz Watch are original and created for demonstration purposes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="rounded-lg border border-amber-400/40 bg-amber-500/10 p-4 text-sm text-amber-200" role="note">
    <p class="font-semibold">Disclaimer</p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-amber-200/80">
      All figures on this site are demonstration data unless a panel is explicitly marked LIVE. Do
      not use this site for trading, investment, navigation or safety-critical decisions. Headlines
      provided via third-party APIs are supplied as-is and are not verified reporting.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-400">
    Read the <a href="/methodology" class="text-cyan-400 underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-2 hover:text-cyan-300">methodology</a>
    or browse the <a href="/blog" class="text-cyan-400 underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-2 hover:text-cyan-300">blog</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
